Step 0 has produced a decisive result: Track A is untenable. The paper’s own equation (6), together with the published conjugating bases, turns recovery of \(a_3\) into a homogeneous finite-field linear system. More strongly, the author’s follow-up paper explicitly says an algebraic-span attack “seems to break” this work. I’m validating the reduction and documenting the rejection; I will not spend a builder/hardening run on a family whose witness is produced by Gaussian elimination.
