codex
Rejected at Step 0; no generator was created.

The paper’s public equation \(w=x_2^{-1}a_3\), with public bases \(Q,S\), becomes

\[
x_i(SwQ^{-1})_{ij}=(SQ^{-1})_{ij}a_j,
\]

a homogeneous linear system with \(d^2\) equations and \(2d\) unknowns. A second identical scaling recovery handles \(v\), then \(a_1=ux_1^{-1}\). The resulting full witness was recovered and exactly verified on 100/100 faithful \(d=8,p=251\) instances in 0.8653 ms per instance.

Thus Track A is false. Track B is also unsuitable because the native dense change-of-basis route exceeds the no-tool operation cap, while exposing transformed matrices would make the shortcut immediate and change the paper’s problem. The author’s [follow-up paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1812.05454) also acknowledges that algebraic-span attacks appear to break the original construction; the general attack is detailed in [Cryptanalysis via Algebraic Spans](https://eprint.iacr.org/2014/041).

Full derivation and evidence: [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1810.08983/REJECTED.md).
